  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The XPath generated for policy queries in the xml database are restrictive and in certain cases will not return matching policies.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Example:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "If a policy specifies an attribute id not usually supplied in the request it will not be matched when it should be (the policy query is built on attributes supplied by the PEP; ie before additional attribute-finding has taken place).  An attribute in the policy which is not specified in the request should always result in a match (since the finder is unable to determine if the policy matches due to lack of information in the request).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The attribute conditions part of the query needs to include an additional clause specifying \"if a policy attribute is not present in the request\".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
