     "body": "<p>The above is still imperfect - there is a distinction between:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>a datastream ID attribute missing in the request; which means the resource is not a datastream, and there should be no policy matching on the datastream attribute</li>\n\t<li>a custom resouce attribute missing in the request; which means the request does not know about the attribute (it will be retrieved later when evaluating); and a policy specifying this attribute should always be matched by the finder.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>But it is probably the best we can do unless a mechanism for specifying attribute lookups to take place before policy finding takes place can be implemented.</p>",
     "created": "10/Apr/11 10:13 AM",
